                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Turns out the biggest threat to humanity wasn't the aliens. It was me being put in charge of its defense.\n\nI'm reviewing this one purely from memory, so the details are a bit fuzzy, but I remember XCOM giving me both good times and some seriously hard ones. Things started off well enough before turning into an absolute mess. I lost squad members, some far more valuable than others, struggled with the game's unforgiving systems, and eventually had to restart my entire campaign after failing to keep up with its pressures.\n\nBut once I finally learned the ropes, things started to click. What began as a desperate struggle for survival gradually turned into me steamrolling my way through the alien invasion, right up to the final mission. Going from barely knowing what the hell I was doing to confidently taking down everything in my path was genuinely satisfying.\n\n7/10. A rough beginning, a rewarding learning curve, and a good time overall. Humanity was in questionable hands, but we got there eventually.",
